<title>USA: Hewlett-Packard sets $1 bln shr buyback.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard sets $1 bln shr buyback.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co said its board on Friday authorized the repurchase of an additional $1 billion of common stock.</p>
<p>The maker of computers, printers and other computer equipment did not set set a date for completing the buyback.</p>
<p>About $230 million remains from earlier stock repurchase authorizations, it said.</p>
<p>Since the beginning of 1994, Hewlett-Packard has repurchased 61.5 million shares.</p>
<p>The company's stock was up 1-5/8 to 54-1/2.  </p>
<p>Separately, the board declared a regular quarterly dividend of $0.12 a share, payable January 15, record December 24.</p>
<p>As of October 31, the company had 1.01 billion shares of common stock outstanding.</p>
</text>
